+/* lane wifi-ax-twt-impl (task-199), FAIL-CLOSED default 0.  TWT is the one
+ * 802.11ax feature the vendor host can enable end-to-end without an
+ * associated client: the user path wal_hipriv_twt_enable accepts only {1,3}
+ * and posts a g0-id1 config event (key 0x035D, one-byte body); the firmware
+ * worker CA 0x41E5A writes ctx+0xDA.bit6 (enable) / bit7 (required) of the
+ * per-module context.  The per-user agreement needs an associated STA (the
+ * RX gate) and is NOT implemented here.
+ *   0 (default) = no 0x035D frame at all - current behaviour, byte-identical
+ *                 to the bench-fired ladder;
+ *   1           = TWT enable (bit0), posted after the VAP start on a
